/* ══ v387 EDIT AUDIOS classification ═══════════════════════════════════════
   TikTok-style edit audio was drowning the ordinary Library. Classification is
   LAYERED, in confidence order, exactly because a filename alone is weak
   evidence:
     1. an explicit category the member (or a previous classification) saved;
     2. explicit provenance metadata when the item came from TikTok;
     3. filename heuristics, and only as a last resort.

   The heuristic is deliberately SCORED and needs two independent signals
   before it will move anything, because a false positive hides a song the
   member expected to find. "the-weeknd-blinding-lights" trips the long-slug
   signal alone and therefore stays in Library, which is the correct outcome.
   Nothing here deletes, copies or rewrites an audio asset -- only which shelf
   it is presented on. */
